    "stem": "Vikram's data are $2$, $6$, $8$, and $12$. He wants the arithmetic mean as the equal-share value of that list.\n\nWhich statements are correct?",
    "item_type": "three_statement",
    "options": {
      "A": "1 and 2 only",
      "B": "1 and 3 only",
      "C": "2 and 3 only",
      "D": "1, 2 and 3"
    },
    "statements": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "The mean is $(2 + 6 + 8 + 12) \\div 4 = 7$, the equal share of the total."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "If the four values shared the total equally, each share would be $7$."
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "The mean is found by multiplying $2$, $6$, $8$, and $12$ instead of dividing their sum by $4$."
      }
